# Slice 3a fix round 3: writer-only exports skip the cursor check (P3)

The new test pins the P3 finding, passed against the unchanged source, and fails when I deliberately break the rule. So `serve!` was already right: only exports with a reader surface get the cursor check.

## Changed files
- `test/yin/vm/ffi/remote_serve_test.cljc` only.

`remote_serve.cljc` was edited only for the temporary mutation and is back to its previous content. Nothing is staged or committed.

## What changed in the test
- **Fixture:** `host-cursor-reader` is now also a writer (`append!` answers ok), while its reader cursors still hold a host object (a fn). The existing reader-surface refusal case is unaffected; that handle is still refused.
- **Test:** the writer-only case in `a-reader-whose-cursors-are-not-portable-is-never-entered` now serves that fixture under a writer-only surface policy, instead of a ring with portable cursors. It asserts:
  - `serve!` admits the handle.
  - Its table entry is exactly `{:handle h, :surface #{:writer}}`.

